  "summary": "One dependency-free TypeScript backend example now persists complete exact intents, operation/destination and original credential bindings before send, supports explicit original-key recovery across processes, and receives signed events with durable deduplication. The generated client preserves the API base prefix, rejects escaped/plaintext remote destinations, bounds network time, protects credential headers, and can obtain a fresh delegated assertion per call. API 3.7.0 documents own-principal versus delegated authentication. Developer starts with this workflow and derives operation-specific retry advice from a generated web-local contract projection. Other recipes and detailed references remain available.",
